From 1b4c342989d8d9cf7a373c49d971922b18c0b9b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI_Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:30:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] server: the lane's logprob takes on every rank, each
 requested id its own logprob, and the build's own fields

Three defects of 0099's prompt logprobs, found on the live 2x RTX PRO 6000 server on 2026-11-05:

- glm cuda: a verify's, shared round's or first token's logprob-row take gathered whole rows through
  every rank, but only prompt steps told the other ranks a collective was due - their next receive read
  logits as the step header and both ranks stopped (TooManyIds). Every take now goes out as a logprob
  step (kind, the rows or, shared, each part's) the other ranks join gather for gather.
- lanes/kernels: a row's requested ids all scored the row's first id's logprob and rank: the kernel
  indexed the id words by the stride the caller had already advanced past. Each id takes its own word
  now; slots past the row's width read as none, so the last row no longer reads past the buffer.
- server: /v1/models' tokenizer_sha256 was 32 raw bytes inside the JSON string; it is hex now, and the
  build names its release, commit, patch stack and backend, the checkpoint's compute dtype (the model
  config's own field first), rope theta, scaling and original context, and the tokenizer's class.

Tests: the two-rank glm-lanes-logprobs runner command (the combined call, a word-for-word repeat, and
logprob streams beside plain ones in shared rounds, picks as the plain run's); topk-extras on the
sample runner (each requested id its own logprob and rank, an id inside the best the best entry's own
word less the normalizer, gaps and ids past the vocabulary none); the build facts' host test.
